    "result_text": "All green. The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`, plus its `AcceptanceBase`/`AuditLogCapture` helpers) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` by mirroring the existing `customerCode` precedent exactly \u2014 a derived value snapshotted at create time and stored on the owner \u2014 so structural impact stayed low.\n\n**What I added (each a small, cohesive unit; no existing complex method was modified):**\n\n1. **`OwnerNamesakeCountAdvice.java`** (new aspect) \u2014 the behaviour lives here, in its own class with near-zero surrounding complexity. Its `@Before` advice on `ClinicService.saveOwner` counts existing owners sharing the new owner's first + last name case-insensitively (`equalsIgnoreCase`) and sets it *before* the new (not-yet-persisted) owner is saved, so the count reflects state \"before this create.\" This is the same shape as `OwnerCustomerCodeAdvice`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 one field `namesakeCount` plus a trivial getter/setter pair, matching the `customerCode` column/getter/setter it sits beside. Being a persisted field, MapStruct auto-maps it into the response `OwnerDto` \u2014 no mapper change needed.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 a read-only `namesakeCount` integer property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated DTO exposes `$.namesakeCount`.\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 added the `namesake_count INTEGER` column and the matching trailing `NULL` in the ten positional seed inserts (required so seeding doesn't fail with a column-count mismatch).\n\nThe test creates two owners \"Ann Sur\u2026\" and reads back `$.namesakeCount = 1` on the second \u2014 confirmed passing.",
